  "note": "日陀罗寺、日陀罗寺佛殿 (native:fanfang/temple_yard, shrine; 番坊 B; daemon/class/lama/master.c's 龙若法王 placed here): a small temple of red-ochre walls with grass along their tops; the great banyan in the middle of the yard, its crown over half of it, air roots grown into trunks, the ground under it sat smooth, the master's cushion there; the bronze bell green with age on its frame in the corner, a water vat, a stone bench, leaves coming down; east the little shrine — the Buddha from 天竺 on his dais, the offering table with butter lamps guttering, cushions, palm-leaf sutras heaped in the corner, a lantern at its door. Old and used: moss in the yard's joints, the wall's plaster fallen in patches, lamp soot over the altar, leaves swept into the corners.",
